1. Data Tidiness

Abridgements
    The cardinal rules of using spreadsheet programs for data:
        Leave the raw data raw - do not change it!
        Put each observation or sample in its own row.
        Put all your variables in columns - the thing that vary between samples
        Have column names be explanatory, but without spaces. (-, _, ...)
        Do not combine multiple pieces of information in one cell.
        Export the cleaned data to a text-based format like CSV (comma-separated values) format.
    Tools like OpenRefine can help you clean your data.

Key Points
    Metadata is key for you and others to be able to work with your data.
    Tabular data needs to be structured to be able to work with it effectively.

